{"title":"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Factoring_and_Midpoint_Substitution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Factoring and Midpoint Substitution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df2fe64c1c244d8efbb77c10bf8ee554b4860a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-19n+99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">perfect square</a>.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1cf9acce28b8ee5dc641709c1e313fd4691ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-19n+99=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"151\" height=\"16\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then rearranging we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7761660c43d00cba6d6890f0cda0e39d259bfbbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-19n+99-x^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"183\" height=\"16\" />. Now from the quadratic formula, \n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f17d0d8cbaf665e7ba3d74740bc72c82635f5fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{19\\pm \\sqrt{4x^2-35}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3df82b441da75db4c0cf4cce7edbd1fc10daf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2-35=q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> for some nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Rearranging gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1d896b0708250c3382bae6a84d24d773b9d1aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x+q)(2x-q)=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db67b835759f90906717fce0f69509fe23f305bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2x+q, 2x-q)=(35, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d388db7aa14bd2737621f3db4b897e9e63ec4ea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/8780242b5627e8a2690424e51e579c8bf40476cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1, 9, 10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e67e80b006a59591cd756895e4c0d514b8e05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+9+10+18=\\boxed{38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c31e930eeb5d3827a9e80f7c8a0e21016b86b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 19x + 99 = k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />. Completing the square, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d928e8c79894c5504989d5f0744c846678ed6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 19/2)^2 + 99 - (19/2)^2 = k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"19\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/24086637dd15ac6af3816e306225cc5c3e583dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 19/2)^2 + 35/4 = k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"19\" />. Multiplying both sides by 4 and rearranging, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/4237bf6d1259d299a860bacda09bc9482fd8a420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2k)^2 - (2x - 19)^2 = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de90f0be436308e631a56a535a79d9f00c79c74e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2k - 2x + 19)(2k + 2x - 19) = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" />. We then proceed as we did in the previous solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84e760e496289679952738cb184bc16b8bbb834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbd841be4e04181821cb5b138cefcb0329c3a5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n-10)^2 &lt; n^2 -19n + 99 &lt; (n-8)^2.\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>So if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84e760e496289679952738cb184bc16b8bbb834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd1e0520edc4954c6bb1aaabf505d2152352ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 -19n + 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square, then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bbea318696aacc4e1a63ef35356b064342d473.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 -19n + 99 = (n-9)^2\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e99f468a9d0856717d34f8258350da274cb3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1ae885b98df1b8d6225182e64809c1305318aff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq n &lt; 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, it is easy to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd1e0520edc4954c6bb1aaabf505d2152352ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 -19n + 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63dbc84b34ac3b13a848f49d0301f67ccc8aec0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ( using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b37e96e2cdde30742eab7ac2724782e6cac8d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 -19n + 99 = (n-10)^2 + n - 1.)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We conclude that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bd53a54d3a5c961df1b06266c6cffa833e8db0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 + 10 + 18 = \\boxed{38}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Factoring_and_Midpoint_Substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Factoring_and_Midpoint_Substitution)\">Solution 4 (Factoring and Midpoint Substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Factoring and Midpoint Substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem states that we want to find integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e53b07f5405e01874a3f0e506d556af4623bb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 - 19n + 99 = k^2 \\text{, for some integer } k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"19\" />\nNotice that the expression can be rewritten to,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f384a2a9ec9fa86b9614702a898f607fa8fdf72a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 - 19n + 18 = k^2 - 81\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4fa699b2a76088f0a1d88b95ebcac27268b10d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n-18)(n-1) = k^2 - 81\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Using midpoint substitution, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2050b6635fe79314b74cfdeefa260e387da7108c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u = n - \\frac{18+1}{2} = n - \\frac{19}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Substituting to the factored expression yields,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4d55f292ec7fd2ef2cf64858109c23bc67f966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(u-\\frac{17}{2}\\right)\\left(u+\\frac{17}{2}\\right) = k^2 - 81\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c1dc4621f7f7db603ab0f56fb26aa2b09d1da2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u^2 - \\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)^2 = k^2 - 81\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/12239155d0bcee7f778227c7f95f1e374be0c781.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u^2 - k^2 = -\\frac{35}{4}\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eec42f8e974af2ca0fb6a37f6f6968b7d62cc22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(u+k)(u-k) = -35\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/9244f8f20c5cb3368ef7c965fc14d483cca5e1e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2u + 2k)(2u - 2k) = -35\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\nNotice the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185089539afe9f3918377ca3c2643ff5db5fe71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 7), (5, -7), (-1, 35)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a9d96b459480d40ac3afe4200fa4668db87e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, -35)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Solving the systems of equations for each factored pair gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db8dbe796ee0462a1b84378066fefdde25f91155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1, 9, 10, 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b0c9e3638d4e08e076e1af515b163acfe15844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 + 10 + 18 = \\boxed{38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"177\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME\" title=\"1999 AIME\">1999 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016224431\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 338/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9416/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.372      1 -total\n 59.86%    7.406      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.41%    4.752      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3034:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016224431 and revision id 287625. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}